\section{Method}
\label{sec:method}

\begin{figure*}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{figures/pipeline.pdf}
\caption{Generational depth estimation pipeline. Seed documents are recursively passed through a generation operator $G_\delta$ to produce a depth chain. Statistical features are fed to the OBD-LightGBM classifier for depth prediction.}
\label{fig:pipeline}
\end{figure*}

\subsection{Problem Formulation}
\label{sec:formulation}

A generation operator $G_\delta$ (LLM + decoding strategy $\delta$) produces successive generations $X \to Y_1 \to \cdots \to Y_K$, where $Y_k = G_\delta(Y_{k-1})$ and $Y_0 \triangleq X$ (Figure~\ref{fig:pipeline}).
This sequence forms a Markov chain.
By the Data Processing Inequality, $I(X; Y_1) \geq I(X; Y_2) \geq \cdots \geq 0$: the original signal degrades monotonically.
Together with Markov chain convergence, this guarantees a finite $\Ktheory$ beyond which adjacent generations are indistinguishable.

We define the operational lower bound:
\begin{equation}
  \Kempirical = \max\{k : \text{CI}_{\text{lower}}^{95\%}(\auc_{k,k+1}) > \theta\},
  \label{eq:kstar}
\end{equation}
where $\theta = 0.60$ is justified by the permutation null distribution (95th percentile $< 0.55$ across all configurations; bootstrap: 1{,}000 resamples).

\subsection{Features and Classifier}
\label{sec:features}

Each document is characterized by a 15-dimensional feature vector (Table~\ref{tab:features}; full definitions in Table~\ref{tab:s5_features}): surprisal moments and derivatives (9~dims), vocabulary diversity (3~dims), and frequency tail statistics (3~dims).
All features are computed from token-level surprisal values via an external scorer model.
Hand-crafted features enable cross-generator transfer without retraining and permit attribution of discriminative power to specific text properties.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\caption{The 15-dimensional feature set.}
\label{tab:features}
\begin{tabular}{lll}
\toprule
\textbf{Group} & \textbf{Feature} & \textbf{Description} \\
\midrule
\multirow{4}{*}{\parbox{1.8cm}{Surprisal\\moments}}
